{"user": "When I had a1, g2, and a3 available earlier, I chose a3 because it felt central. But why did that particular move actually force White to pass right after, while a1 or g2 would not have?", "user_ts": "2026-08-10T23:59:06.549404+00:00", "assistant": "Because **a3 changed White\u2019s mobility**, not because it was \u201ccentral.\u201d\n\nFor White to have a move, an empty square must let White place a disc that **sandwiches at least one Black line ending in a White disc**.\n\nAfter **Black a3**, the remaining empties did **not** give White any such sandwich, so White had **zero legal moves** and had to pass.\n\nIf Black had played **a1** or **g2** instead, the flips would have left White with at least one legal bracket somewhere, so White would not pass.\n\nSo the key idea: **a3 was a tempo/mobility move** \u2014 it removed White\u2019s legal replies and let you move again.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-10T23:59:06.549404+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-10T23:59:11.549404+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Move Verdict": 1, "Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 2, "General Principle": 2, "Board Report": 2, "Negative Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Move Verdict": 0.3333333333333333, "Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Line":